-- title:
--   Extending a Hecke character across a good prime r
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero; let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, let $N \geq 1$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$ and $r \nmid N$. For a set $T$ of naturals write $\mathbb T^T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` at primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin T$ together with the operators `heckeULin` at primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin T$, and let `heckeAlgebra.T` denote the generator attached to $\ell$. Given ring homomorphisms $\theta \colon \mathbb T^{S} \to \mathcal O/\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ and $\chi_0 \colon \mathbb T^{S \cup \{r\}} \to \mathcal O$ such that the residue of $\chi_0(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ lying outside $S$ and outside $S \cup \{r\}$, the conclusion asserts the existence of a type $\mathcal O'$ carrying the same list of assumptions (commutative domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, finite residue field, characteristic zero), together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure making $\mathcal O'$ a finite $\mathcal O$-module with $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O'$ a local homomorphism, such that $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O'$ is injective and there is a ring homomorphism $\chi \colon \mathbb T^{S} \to \mathcal O'$ with $\chi(T_\ell)$ equal to the image of $\chi_0(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$ and outside $S \cup \{r\}$, and with the residue of $\chi(t)$ equal to the image of $\theta(t)$ under the induced map of residue fields, for every $t \in \mathbb T^{S}$.
--
--   This is the statement that a Hecke character of the smaller (more anemic) weight-two Hecke algebra, congruent to a given residual character $\theta$ away from $r$, can be extended, after a finite extension of the coefficient ring, to the Hecke algebra including the operator at the good prime $r$, with reduction exactly $\theta$; in particular $\chi(T_r)$ reduces to $\theta(T_r)$. It is the form of the redundancy of $T_r$ used in the construction of auxiliary-level modular forms, and is invoked in the vanishing statements for cohomology classes and for maps out of the auxiliary-level space.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeAlgebra_exists_ringHom_apply_T_eq_of_insert_of_residue_eq.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
